.verify-*.mjs

# Large / generated
screenshots/
*.mp4
*.webm
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Orca pairing tokens
orca-pair-code.txt
orca-pair-code.html
.keep-awake.pid
keep-awake.log

# 375MB binaries — never commit
orca-linux.AppImage
orca-linux.AppImage.bak.*

# Private Events Bot ops — EVERY DEMIGOD-EVENTS.* file is a full/partial copy of the events SoR
# (offer/RSVP/contact PII). Broad wildcard: the earlier .json.* patterns missed the pre-<label>-<ts>
# snapshots (pre-calpurge/pre-rungate — the suffix is BEFORE .json), which held 12+11 real contact
# emails and were commit-eligible. DEMIGOD-EVENTS.* catches the main file, atomic-write temps
# (.json.tmp.<pid>, .json.bak.<pid>), .corrupt/.archive, AND the pre-* snapshots. Never commit any.
DEMIGOD-EVENTS.json
DEMIGOD-EVENTS.*
events-bot-outbox/
# Leads SoR + its derivatives hold founder/candidate PII -- never commit. Untracked today, so
# ignoring now keeps it out of history cleanly (no scrub needed). The .archive.jsonl is written by
# ingestSubmission's cap (46a1c30); .corrupt.* by loadInbox's preserve-on-corruption guard (665d0da).
DEMIGOD-SUBMISSIONS-INBOX.json
DEMIGOD-SUBMISSIONS-INBOX.json.archive.jsonl
DEMIGOD-SUBMISSIONS-INBOX.json.corrupt.*
DEMIGOD-INBOX-REPORT.json
# Private local candidate CRM (messages, resumes, contact details); never stage.
talent-crm/
# Private YC directory snapshot; public map data is a separate licensed projection.
DEMIGOD-SF-STARTUPS.json
# Per-person meeting prep contains private contact/context; keep other demigod-ops sources trackable.
demigod-ops/*-PREP-*.md
# Founder/candidate outreach is private operational data: contacts, drafts, trackers, and send
# history. Only the two generic templates are source; everything else stays local.
demigod-outreach/*
!demigod-outreach/template-dm.md
!demigod-outreach/template-dm-engineer.md
# Root-level send logs (stray copies outside demigod-outreach/) hold DM transport evidence.
dm-send-log.txt
# Generated signal manifest may contain a real receipt capability URL.
SIGNAL-THEATER.json
DEMIGOD-PROOF-LOG.json
DEMIGOD-PROOF-LOG.json.corrupt.*
# Private matching/outreach state and generated intro/invoice packets.
DEMIGOD-MATCHES.json*
DEMIGOD-OUTREACH.json*
demigod-ops/intros/*
!demigod-ops/intros/.gitkeep
demigod-ops/invoices/
# Board corruption backups (old .bak/.corrupt snapshots hold real founder handles/emails) and grok
# conversation scratch (contains a personal email). Cruft/scratch, never meant to be committed.
DEMIGOD-BOARD.corrupt*
DEMIGOD-BOARD.CORRUPT*
grok-input.txt
grok-snapshot.txt
grok-tail.txt

# Firecrawl secrets
.env.firecrawl
.firecrawl-key
.config/firecrawl/


# Agent status scratch with a personal email (ORCA pair status).
ORCA-PAIR-EMAIL-STATUS.txt

# Board + pairs SoRs and their regenerable runtime outputs — hold candidate/role data (anonymized but
# identifiable once real inbound starts). Untracked today (0 real, sample-only), so ignoring now keeps
# them out of history cleanly — same proactive rule as the inbox/leads SoRs above. The tracked symlink
# demigod-board.json -> DEMIGOD-BOARD.json stays (it is a pointer, no data). NB: DEMIGOD-BOARD.corrupt*
# above is uppercase and missed the lowercase demigod-board.corrupt-* backups (real data at corrupt-time).
DEMIGOD-BOARD.json
DEMIGOD-BOARD.json.*
DEMIGOD-PAIRS.json
DEMIGOD-PAIRS.json.*
DEMIGOD-BOARD-HONESTY.json
DEMIGOD-BOARD-AUDIT.jsonl
DEMIGOD-BOARD-CDN.json
DEMIGOD-BOARD-PUBLIC.json
demigod-board.corrupt*
demigod-foot-core.b64

# More SoRs a `git add -A --dry-run` (cycle 415) proved committable — the earlier per-file check missed
# them. DEMIGOD-LEADS.json holds REAL founder/candidate PII (untracked today = active risk, not latent).
# DEMIGOD-EVENTS.* (dot) missed hyphenated DEMIGOD-EVENTS-API.json + lowercase demigod-events-data.json;
# DEMIGOD-BOARD.json.* (uppercase) missed lowercase demigod-board.json.bak-*. All never-tracked -> clean.
DEMIGOD-LEADS.json
DEMIGOD-LEADS.json.*
DEMIGOD-PILOTS.json
DEMIGOD-PILOTS.json.*
DEMIGOD-REFERRALS.json
DEMIGOD-REFERRALS.json.*
DEMIGOD-EVENTS-API.json
demigod-events-data.json
demigod-events-data.json.*
demigod-board.json.bak*
*.mjs.bak

# Browser/system dotfile dirs (the repo IS /home/potter, so `git add -A` would stage them). Agent
# dotfiles (.grok/.codex/.cursor/.claude) were ignored earlier; these hold browser session state/cookies
# (.mozilla — incl auth for the :9223 Designer), Wine app data, and cert DBs. Defense-in-depth so an
# accidental `git add -A` of the home dir can't commit session tokens or system cruft. (cycle 421)
.mozilla/
.wine/
.pki/
DEMIGOD-ROLE-LEDGER.json

# Personal-contact operational artifacts: call packs, day cards, countdowns, and a Gmail draft
# that carries a real third-party address. These are untracked siblings of files already tracked
# here (DOUGLAS-RUN-OF-SHOW.md, PILOT-LOG.md), so a bulk `git add -A` by any agent would sweep
# them into history. Same private-operational-data rule as demigod-outreach/* above.
demigod-ops/DOUGLAS-*
# No negation re-opening this path: a `!` exception inside a PII-protected directory is a
# hole the privacy gate rejects, and it bought nothing — DOUGLAS-RUN-OF-SHOW.md was already
# tracked, and .gitignore never untracks an existing file.
demigod-ops/SEND-QUEUE-PRIORITIZED.md
# Inbox triage SoR — small today, grows with real submissions.
DEMIGOD-INBOX-TRIAGE.json

# Embedded git repo — would land as a broken gitlink, not real content.
hahahacks-2026/

# Large binaries: GitHub rejects >100MB and these are re-downloadable artifacts.
*.AppImage
*.AppImage.v*

# Private outreach working state: aging-startup targets derived from the role ledger.
# Company names + observation dates + human notes. Never committed, same posture as LEADS/BOARD.
DEMIGOD-TARGETS.json

# Ship staging: build output and duplicated docs, regenerated by dasha-ship.mjs.
# Tracked once by an over-broad `git add -A`; it is not source.
.tmp-dasha-ship/

# Wrangler's per-project state and deploy logs. Not source, and a `git add -A` in a repo rooted at
# $HOME would stage 15 of them. Audited before ignoring rather than assumed: the logs contain no
# credential values — the only matches are the literal string `grant_type=refresh_token` and file
# paths ending `oauth/.env`. The real Cloudflare OAuth token lives at ~/.config/.wrangler at 0600,
# under the already-ignored .config/ path. So this is hygiene, not an exposure fix.
.wrangler/

# Media sources are the originals, recoverable from the site; only the built
# deliverables and their manifest belong in git.
dasha-media/src/
